= entry .Serialization   the supertype of the encodings, and the home of `Serialization.Error`
-   detail
+   detail

-       Each encoding is a sealed subtrait of `Serialization` — `Base64`, `Base32`, `Hex`,
-       `Octal`, `Quaternary` and `Binary` — used only as a type argument, to `serialize[Base64]`
-       or `Alphabet[Hex]`, and never instantiated.
+       Cada codificación es un subtrait sellado de `Serialization` —`Base64`, `Base32`, `Hex`,
+       `Octal`, `Quaternary` y `Binary`—, que solo se usa como argumento de tipo, para
+       `serialize[Base64]` o `Alphabet[Hex]`, y nunca se instancia.

-   refer monotonous.Serialization.Error
+   refer monotonous.Serialization.Error

-   entry .Error   raised when text to be deserialized holds a character not in the alphabet
+   entry .Error   se lanza cuando el texto que se va a deserializar contiene un carácter que no está en el alfabeto

-     detail
+     detail

-         Error `↯/s.61.1`: _the character `char` at `position` was not valid_. Raised by `deserialize`
-         and by the streaming deserializer when a character is neither one of the alphabet's
-         own nor one of its tolerated alternatives. A strict alphabet raises it for the other
-         case of a letter, where a tolerant one would accept it.
+         Error `↯/s.61.1`: _the character `char` at `position` was not valid_. Lo lanzan
+         `deserialize` y el deserializador de flujos cuando un carácter no es ni uno de los
+         propios del alfabeto ni una de sus alternativas toleradas. Un alfabeto estricto lo
+         lanza para la otra caja de una letra, que uno tolerante aceptaría.

-         ```scala
+         ```scala

-         import soundness.*
+         import soundness.*

-         import alphabets.base32LowerCase
+         import alphabets.base32LowerCase

-         capture[Serialization.Error](t"AAAQEA4?DQKAYB7H5737Q====".deserialize[Base32])
+         capture[Serialization.Error](t"AAAQEA4?DQKAYB7H5737Q====".deserialize[Base32])

-         // Serialization.Error(7, '?')
+         // Serialization.Error(7, '?')

-         ```
+         ```

-     entry #position   the index, from zero, of the invalid character in the text
-     entry #char       the invalid character
+     entry #position   el índice, empezando por cero, del carácter no válido en el texto
+     entry #char       el carácter no válido

